 Plan: Smart Image Embedding — Docling-Gated, Resized, Store-for-Retrieval                                                                                          │
     │                                                                                                                                                                    │
     │ Context                                                                                                                                                            │
     │                                                                                                                                                                    │
     │ Ingesting a 25-page OCR PDF takes 10+ minutes because every PDF page is embedded as an image regardless of content. Jina v4 uses a 3.8B-param Qwen2.5-VL backbone  │
     │ — each image is split into 28x28 tiles at 10 tokens/tile, so a single 600px page costs ~4,840 tokens running through the full decoder. At 100K TPM this throttles  │
     │ hard.                                                                                                                                                              │
     │                                                                                                                                                                    │
     │ Goal: Three changes to cut ingestion time from 10+ minutes to under 1 minute:                                                                                      │
     │ 1. Content-gate image embedding via Docling layout analysis — only embed visual pages                                                                              │
     │ 2. Resize images to 400px max before embedding — reduce token cost per image by ~75%                                                                               │
     │ 3. Store thumbnails for text-only pages — available at retrieval time, zero embedding cost                                                                         │
     │                                                                                                                                                                    │
     │ No backward compatibility needed — agile development, clean sweep.                                                                                                 │
     │                                                                                                                                                                    │
     │ Why Docling Over PyMuPDF Heuristics                                                                                                                                │
     │                                                                                                                                                                    │
     │ Docling (already installed at v2.76.0) uses RT-DETR trained on DocLayNet (17 element types, mAP 0.77). PyMuPDF heuristics miss embedded figures, borderless        │
     │ tables, and formulas entirely. Current code already runs Docling per-page for OCR — the new approach runs it once on the whole PDF for both OCR and layout         │
     │ classification.                                                                                                                                                    │
